&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;m_8220454926977230902gmail-docs-internal-guid-9a9f34f4-7fff-014a-c97c-98ca90610a47&quot;&gt;Algolia is the retrieval intelligence layer that turns intent into trusted, decision-grade outcomes. Powering more than 1.7 trillion queries a year for over 18,000 customers with millisecond latency and 99.999% reliability, we are the recognized leader for Search and Product Discovery by top industry analyst firms. The Algolia platform turns a company&#39;s products, content, and business rules into data that humans, applications and AI agents can act upon. The result is trusted customer experiences with stronger conversions for measurable business impact.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Partner Account Manager to grow Algolia’s partner ecosystem across &lt;strong&gt;Italy, Spain and the Netherlands&lt;/strong&gt;, with a primary focus on Italy and the Netherlands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of our Global Alliances team, you’ll build strong relationships with system integrators, digital agencies and other services partners. You’ll bring partners and Algolia teams together around shared opportunities, helping customers create better digital experiences while generating pipeline and revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to make an impact across a diverse territory: you’ll help develop the partner ecosystem in Italy and Spain while deepening established relationships in the Netherlands. You’ll have room to shape your approach to each market, supported by a collaborative team and a shared focus on growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Examples of partners include Atoms, Reply, Accenture, Kega, SQLI, Ogilvy, VASS, Shopify and commercetools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a revenue quota based on the business generated by your partners across Italy, Spain and the Netherlands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute a partner strategy for Italy, Spain and the Netherlands, prioritizing the opportunities with the greatest potential for growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted relationships with key system integrators and digital agencies, from sales and marketing teams to alliances leaders and executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create joint business plans and coordinate sales and marketing initiatives that generate qualified pipeline and revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help partners understand Algolia’s value, build their capabilities and position our solutions with their customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Algolia at partner meetings, events and other activities across the territory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least &lt;strong&gt;5 years of experience&lt;/strong&gt; in partner management, alliances, channel sales or a comparable role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience carrying a quota, with a track record of driving pipeline and revenue through partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and growing relationships with system integrators, digital agencies or other services partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong ability to identify opportunities, develop joint plans and turn them into results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidence working across sales, marketing and technical teams, both internally and within partner organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to balance strategic thinking with a hands-on approach to execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and relationship-building skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fluency in English and Italian&lt;/strong&gt;, both written and spoken. Additional languages, particularly Dutch or Spanish, are a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel regularly across the territory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Algolia does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, military status, veteran status, disability status, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, or any other characteristic protected by law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The annual total cash compensation range (base salary and commission) for this role reflects market pay data within this location. The exact compensation offered for this role may vary depending on specific location and job-related knowledge, technical skills, and experience; and is only one part of our Total Rewards philosophy to compensate and recognize employees for their work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;On-Target Earnings Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€139.500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€174.500 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FLEXIBLE WORKPLACE STRATEGY:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Algolia’s flexible workplace model is designed to empower all Algolians to fulfill our mission to power search and discovery with ease. We place an emphasis on an individual’s impact, contribution, and output, over their physical location. Algolia is a high-trust environment and many of our team members have the autonomy to choose where they want to work and when.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a global presence with offices in Paris, NYC, London, Sydney and Bucharest, however we also offer many of our team members the option to work remotely either as fully remote or hybrid-remote employees.&lt;strong&gt; Positions listed as &quot;Remote&quot; are only available for remote work within the specified country. Positions listed within a specific city are only available in that location - depending on the role it may be available with either a hybrid-remote or in-office schedule.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WE’RE LOOKING FOR SOMEONE WHO CAN LIVE OUR VALUES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GRIT&lt;/strong&gt; - Problem-solving and perseverance capability in an ever-changing and growing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TRUST &lt;/strong&gt;- Willingness to trust our co-workers and to take ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CANDOR&lt;/strong&gt; - Ability to receive and give constructive feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CARE&lt;/strong&gt; - Genuine care about other team members, our clients and the decisions we make in the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HUMILITY&lt;/strong&gt; - Aptitude for learning from others, putting ego aside.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for talented, passionate people to help build the world’s best search and discovery technology. We value autonomy, diversity, and collaboration. We’re committed to creating an inclusive workplace where everyone is respected and supported—regardless of race, age, ancestry, religion, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, marital status, color, veteran status, disability, or socioeconomic background.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;IMPORTANT NOTICE FOR CANDIDATES - Recruitment Fraud Notice&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’ve recently seen an increase in recruitment scams targeting job seekers. To help protect yourself, please keep the following in mind:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our open positions may appear on third-party job boards, but the &lt;strong&gt;best way to apply safely&lt;/strong&gt; is directly through our &lt;strong&gt;careers page&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All genuine communication from Algolia will come from an ----- email address. If you receive an email from someone claiming to work at Algolia who does not have an ----- email address, please do not respond or share any personal information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We’ll &lt;strong&gt;never ask for payments, purchases, or financial details&lt;/strong&gt; during the hiring process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;READY TO APPLY?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you share our values and our enthusiasm for building the world’s best search &amp;amp; discovery technology, we’d love to review your application!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;section class=&quot;block&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;The role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Technical and consumption strategist for complex, multi-stakeholder opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;block&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead complex consumption-based sales cycles across technical, executive and economic stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape usage forecasts, adoption plans, POV success criteria and expansion paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with AEs on qualification, value messaging and consumption risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the technical DRI for complex evaluations, workshops, audits, tenders and value-stream assessments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own architecture, technical risk, success plan inputs and the technical path to expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply strong DevSecOps, CI/CD, cloud and AI fluency to the customer problem, integrating architecture, security and operational considerations in complex environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;block&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consumption experience: Leading complex consumption motions through discovery, POV, production adoption and value realization, including engaging executives and budget owners and managing trade-offs when usage changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical experience: Proven hands-on depth across the DevSecOps lifecycle, including CI/CD at scale, Kubernetes, application security testing and infrastructure as code, and the ability to design, size and troubleshoot self-managed and on-premises deployments alongside cloud and hybrid architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience with consumption-based, cloud, AI, platform or usage-metered products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A solid understanding of adoption curves, usage forecasting, economic buyers and procurement friction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to connect technical architecture to expansion, renewal and long-term value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to diagnose whether the customer can realize value, not just whether the solution can technically work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to make technical and commercial trade-offs when usage is uncertain or changing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to use customer evidence to influence deal strategy and account planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Motivation from long-term customer value, adoption and expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Energy for complex, multi-stakeholder buying decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A commitment to raising the technical and commercial bar for peers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel at least 25%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Languages to include English, Arabic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;block team&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Solutions Architecture team sits within GitLab Sales and partners with Account Executives, Customer Success and Product to help customers adopt GitLab and grow their usage over time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We act as technical advisors across the full software delivery lifecycle: DevOps, CI/CD, cloud-native platforms, security and software supply chain, and AI-native development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab sells in a consumption-based model, so our work does not end at the proof of value. We map how customers will use GitLab, prove value with evidence, and stay close through production adoption and expansion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We share what we learn, coach each other, and care about measurable customer outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-CM1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation &amp;amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/learning-and-development/growth-and-development/&quot;&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#parental-leave&quot;&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from &lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/#examples-of-select-underrepresented-groups&quot;&gt;underrepresented groups&lt;/a&gt; are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines: &lt;/strong&gt;GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/candidate-faq/recruitment-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; Your privacy is important to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id=&quot;an-overview-of-this-role&quot; data-lfile-container=&quot;21ea07e5-ded4-47e8-ad92-4ca7b7d6be35&quot; data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Corporate Development Director, you&#39;ll help influence how GitLab invests to win: what we build, what we buy, where we partner, and what we should not pursue. This role sits within the Corporate Development &amp;amp; Strategic Partnerships team, reporting to the VP, Corporate Development &amp;amp; Strategic Partnerships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role straddles strategy and M&amp;amp;A engagements. You&#39;ll lead research that frames GitLab&#39;s options: mapping the markets in and around our AI-powered DevSecOps platform, testing where we have a right to win, and turning that into clear recommendations for the executive team. When the answer is to acquire, you&#39;ll drive the deal process end to end, from outreach through close and integration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success here is not measured by deal count. It looks like sharper strategic choices: a well-reasoned point of view on our priority markets, investment theses that product and executive leaders rely on, acquisitions that speed up the roadmap when buying is the right answer, and an educated no when it isn&#39;t. You&#39;ll own the wider market perspective rather than individual product categories, and work with the team&#39;s Analyst on the research behind it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;strategy-and-research&quot;&gt;Strategy and research&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the wider market view.&lt;/strong&gt; Research the broader market GitLab competes in, beyond specific product categories: competitive dynamics, AI-native entrants, technology shifts and where value is moving. Collaborate with the team&#39;s Analyst on the research and turn the findings into a clear point of view on where GitLab should play.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build an investment thesis for each focus area.&lt;/strong&gt; Work with Product and Engineering leaders to define the problems worth solving, the capabilities GitLab needs, and what it would cost in time and money to get there on our own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the competitive and landscape view.&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain market maps and a current read on GitLab&#39;s competitors: their strategy, product direction, positioning, pricing, and M&amp;amp;A and funding activity. Produce competitor analyses that show where we lead, where we&#39;re exposed and how rivals are likely to move. Flag shifts by competitors, hyperscalers and AI labs that change our options, and bring the implications to Product and the executive team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define where GitLab should not play.&lt;/strong&gt; Identify adjacencies that dilute focus and markets where the economics or competition work against us. Make the case for a no with the same rigor as a yes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;build-buy-or-partner&quot;&gt;Build, buy or partner&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Run the build, buy, partner analysis.&lt;/strong&gt; For each strategic gap, compare the options side by side on speed, cost, risk, control and strategic fit, and bring a clear recommendation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deliver strategic clarity to&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;executives and the Board.&lt;/strong&gt; Produce short strategy memos/decks and business cases that set out the decision, the trade-offs and what we give up with each path.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Feed company strategy and planning.&lt;/strong&gt; Bring an outside-in view of the market and the inorganic options available into annual and long-range planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work hand in hand with Strategic Partnerships.&lt;/strong&gt; When partnering is the right answer, frame the opportunity and hand it to the partnership owner with a clear thesis. When it isn&#39;t, explain why.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;deal-execution-and-integration&quot;&gt;Deal execution and integration&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own end-to-end deal process management.&lt;/strong&gt; Validate target fit against GitLab&#39;s our target profile, product roadmap and other criteria, and build the acquisition rationale and business case. Drive our M&amp;amp;A process from intro call through the various steps through to closing and integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evaluate the deal.&lt;/strong&gt; Develop valuation, commercial integrity assessment, impact on GitLab&#39;s business and provide negotiations assistance to the VP and the executive team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead cross-functional diligence.&lt;/strong&gt; Run pre-LOI validation and diligence across Product, Engineering, Security, Finance, Legal and People, and communicate findings clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive deal documents with Legal.&lt;/strong&gt; Prepare NDAs, LOIs and purchase agreements with GitLab Legal and outside counsel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own integration outcomes.&lt;/strong&gt; Lead post-acquisition integration as the DRI, measured against the roadmap and business goals in the business case. Bring lessons learned back into the strategy work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the external network.&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain relationships with founders, executives, investors, bankers and advisors that bring us early insight and pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-bring&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategy and deal experience.&lt;/strong&gt; 8+ years across corporate development, corporate strategy, strategy consulting or technology investing, including 5+ years leading acquisitions end to end in enterprise software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Structured strategic thinking.&lt;/strong&gt; You form a point of view from incomplete information, test it against data, and change your mind when the evidence says so. You&#39;re as comfortable recommending that we stay out of a market as that we enter it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market research depth.&lt;/strong&gt; Skilled in market sizing, competitive analysis and landscape mapping, and in turning research into a recommendation, not a report.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deal craft.&lt;/strong&gt; Skilled in valuation, financial modeling, deal structuring, negotiation and integration planning, with experience across varied consideration structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical fluency.&lt;/strong&gt; A working understanding of software development, DevSecOps and the AI landscape, enough to hold substantive conversations with product and engineering leaders about roadmaps and architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clear executive communication.&lt;/strong&gt; You write short, decision-ready updates and present trade-offs plainly to executives and the Board, in an async-first environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Influence without authority.&lt;/strong&gt; You build trust across Product, Engineering, Finance and Legal and move decisions forward across functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership with collaboration.&lt;/strong&gt; You own the strategic view and the recommendation, and partner closely with the team&#39;s Analyst on research and analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&lt;/strong&gt; familiarity with the DevSecOps, security, AI and open source ecosystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You value the &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/all-remote/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;all remote&lt;/a&gt; lifestyle and share our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/values/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;values&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Corporate Development &amp;amp; Strategic Partnerships team helps GitLab decide how to grow beyond what we build on our own. We own inorganic strategy: acquisitions, strategic partnerships with hyperscalers and AI labs, and the research that tells us which to pursue and which to pass on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We work across Product, Engineering, Finance, Legal and the executive group. We set direction and do the detailed work ourselves, with a high degree of ownership and transparency in a fully remote, asynchronous environment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The base salary range for this role’s listed level is currently for residents of the&amp;nbsp;United States only. This range is intended to reflect the role&#39;s base salary rate in locations throughout the US.&amp;nbsp;Grade level and salary ranges are determined through interviews and a review of education, experience, knowledge, skills, abilities of the applicant, equity with other team members, alignment with market data,&amp;nbsp;and geographic location.&amp;nbsp;The base salary range does not include any bonuses, equity, or benefits. See more information on our &lt;a class=&quot;waffle-rich-text-link&quot; href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-link=&quot;https://bit.ly/GLBeneUS&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#1155cc;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:underline;font-family:&#39;&#39;Arial&#39;&#39;;font-style:normal;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;&quot;&gt;benefits&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-formula-bar-text-style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:none;font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;;font-style:normal;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;&quot;&gt; and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;waffle-rich-text-link&quot; href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/stock-options/&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-link=&quot;https://bit.ly/GLequity&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#1155cc;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:underline;font-family:&#39;&#39;Arial&#39;&#39;;font-style:normal;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;&quot;&gt;equity&lt;/a&gt;. Sales roles are also eligible for incentive pay targeted at up to 100% of the offered base salary.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;United States Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$168,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$285,600 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation &amp;amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/learning-and-development/growth-and-development/&quot;&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#parental-leave&quot;&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from &lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/#examples-of-select-underrepresented-groups&quot;&gt;underrepresented groups&lt;/a&gt; are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines: &lt;/strong&gt;GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/candidate-faq/recruitment-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; Your privacy is important to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;𝗪𝗵𝗮𝘁 𝗠𝗮𝗸𝗲𝘀 𝗖𝗹𝗼𝘂𝗱𝗯𝗲𝗱𝘀 𝗨𝗻𝗶𝗾𝘂𝗲&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cloudbeds.com/&quot;&gt;Cloudbeds&lt;/a&gt;, we&#39;re not just building software, we&#39;re transforming hospitality. Our platform powers hotels across 150 countries, processing billions in bookings annually. From boutique properties to large hotel groups, we help hoteliers transform operations and uplevel their commercial strategy through a unified platform that integrates with hundreds of partners. And we do it with a completely remote team. Imagine working alongside global innovators to build AI-powered solutions that solve hoteliers&#39; biggest challenges. Since our founding in 2012, we&#39;ve continually been recognized for excellence, most recently earning top honors at the 2026 HotelTechAwards for Best Hotel Management Software and landing on Deloitte&#39;s Technology Fast 500 again, but we&#39;re just getting started.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;𝗟𝗼𝗰𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Remote&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;𝗛𝗼𝘄 𝗬𝗼𝘂&#39;𝗹𝗹 𝗠𝗮𝗸𝗲 𝗮𝗻 𝗜𝗺𝗽𝗮𝗰𝘁:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an 𝗔𝗰𝗰𝗼𝘂𝗻𝘁 𝗠𝗮𝗻𝗮𝗴𝗲𝗿, you will be part of the Customer Success team. AMs will be expected to actively manage a portfolio of customers with an estimated value of $500,000 - $1,000,000 USD with the goal of building strong customer relationships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our AM Team is responsible for identifying upsell opportunities for ACV expansion and minimizing customer churn. AMs will act as the first point of contact for all things related to Cloudbeds. They are responsible for guiding clients through their customer journey while providing recommendations on how to best improve their business in order to achieve success. As an AM you will make the motto &quot;more reservations, happier guests&quot; a reality by providing strategic guidance to our customers around the world and helping them achieve their &quot;Success Outcomes.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;𝗪𝗵𝗮𝘁 𝗬𝗼𝘂 𝗕𝗿𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝘁𝗼 𝘁𝗵𝗲 𝗧𝗲𝗮𝗺:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the customer&#39;s &quot;success outcomes&quot; and work with them to achieve them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the main point of contact for all things related to Cloudbeds and help escalate urgent support tickets, amongst other things&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Achieve net dollar retention goals through identifying upsell opportunities and implementing proactive churn reduction strategies in order to help Cloudbeds obtain net negative churn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use a consultative approach to drive product engagement, customer &quot;stickiness&quot;, and package growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze customer data to improve customer utilization and engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage customer escalations related to the strategic use of Cloudbeds software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Seek to promote the value of the product and identify new opportunities to upsell additional services and products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review customer complaints and concerns and seek to improve all aspects of the customer experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a detailed understanding of products and services, assist customers with questions, and suggest the best products for their needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather client feedback and requirements for future releases of the software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use training materials to keep up-to-date with the latest system updates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a &quot;strategic partner&quot; to assigned portfolio of customers, utilizing hospitality industry knowledge to provide insight and recommendations to optimize product performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of the hospitality industry - continuously staying updated on industry trends, strategies, and best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;𝗪𝗵𝗮𝘁 𝗦𝗲𝘁𝘀 𝗬𝗼𝘂 𝗨𝗽 𝗳𝗼𝗿 𝗦𝘂𝗰𝗰𝗲𝘀𝘀:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional ability to communicate and foster positive business relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of customers&#39; concerns and thoughts regarding the use of products, and the ability to troubleshoot as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to communicate, present, and influence credibly and effectively at all levels of the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to clearly communicate &amp;amp; synthesize customer details (needs, feedback, concerns, opportunities, etc.) internally to multiple departments (Sales, Support, Product, Marketing, Design).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage multiple projects at a time while paying strict attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent listening, negotiation, and presentation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated and able to thrive in a results-driven environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Natural relationship builder with integrity, reliability, and maturity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives in hyper-growth work environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent time and project management skills; always looking to improve inefficient processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing accounts within the European hospitality market is a significant plus, given the concentration of customers in this region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in both English and German is required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #ffffff;&quot;&gt;#LI-PC1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;𝗪𝗼𝗿𝗸 𝗔𝘂𝘁𝗵𝗼𝗿𝗶𝘇𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻: Please note that applicants must be currently authorized to work in the location where the position is located without requiring visa sponsorship. At this time, Cloudbeds is unable to provide sponsorship for work visas.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;𝗪𝗵𝗮𝘁 𝘁𝗼 𝗘𝘅𝗽𝗲𝗰𝘁 - 𝗬𝗼𝘂𝗿 𝗝𝗼𝘂𝗿𝗻𝗲𝘆 𝘄𝗶𝘁𝗵 𝗨𝘀&lt;/p&gt;
